  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 15, 2026, a violent altercation on a Virar-Churchgate local train in Mumbai resulted in the injury of an uninvolved passenger. According to reports, two individuals were engaged in a fight while the train was traveling near Andheri station. During the dispute, a knife was thrown that struck 53-year-old Suresh Sharma in the chest rather than its intended target. The train was subsequently halted at Bandra station after passengers utilized the emergency alarm to alert authorities. Law enforcement officials have since taken the accused, Shiva Gaikwad, into custody following the incident. The event has drawn attention due to safety concerns regarding commuter violence on the city's rail network, prompting investigations into the conduct of the passengers involved during the transit journey.",
